sanctions-au is an unofficial, independent tool. It is not affiliated with, endorsed or approved
by the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, the Australian Border Force, the Department of
Home Affairs or the Commonwealth of Australia.

This software contains no list data. `sanctions-au refresh` downloads, or imports, two published
datasets, and screens only against the copy you hold:

* DFAT Consolidated List: published by the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade at
  https://www.dfat.gov.au/international-relations/security/sanctions/consolidated-list
* ABF Register of Sanctioned Sponsors: published by the Australian Border Force at
  https://www.abf.gov.au/about-us/what-we-do/sponsor-sanctions/register-of-sanctioned-sponsors
  The page states that it is published under subsection 140K(4) of the Migration Act 1958.

The reuse licences and terms of both publications have NOT been checked by the authors of this
package. Check them before redistributing a snapshot or a result derived from one. The ABF register
includes the names of individuals who are sole-trader sponsors; treat results as personal
information where they identify a person.

The ABF register page fills its table from an undocumented endpoint of the ABF's own site. The
refresh command makes the same two requests as the page, once per refresh, identifying itself as
sanctions-au. That endpoint may change or be withdrawn without notice, in which case a refresh
fails and keeps the previous data.
